<P STYLE="font: bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-transform: uppercase; text-align: center"><A NAME="a_012"></A>Description of
the Additional Tier 1 Securities</P>

<P STYLE="font: bold 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-transform: uppercase; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in"><I>The following is a summary of certain terms
of the Additional Tier 1 Securities. It supplements the description of the general terms of the Capital Securities of any series we may
issue contained in the accompanying prospectus under the heading &ldquo;Description of Capital Securities&rdquo; and &ldquo;Description
of Certain Provisions Relating to Debt Securities and Capital Securities&rdquo;. If there is any inconsistency between the following summary
and the description in the accompanying prospectus, the following summary governs.</I></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.5in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>General</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The following is a summary of certain terms of
the Fixed Rate Reset Additional Tier 1 Securities offered hereby (referred to herein as the &ldquo;<B>Additional Tier 1 Securities</B>&rdquo;).
The summary set forth below does not purport to be complete and is subject to, and qualified in its entirety by reference to, the Capital
Securities Indenture dated as of March 6, 2014 (the &ldquo;<B>Base Indenture</B>&rdquo;), between us as issuer and The Bank of New York
Mellon, acting through its London Branch as trustee (the &ldquo;<B>Trustee</B>&rdquo;), as supplemented by a Tenth Supplemental Indenture
which we expect to be dated as of the Issue Date (the &ldquo;<B>Tenth Supplemental Indenture</B>&rdquo; and, together with the Base Indenture,
the &ldquo;<B>Indenture</B>&rdquo;), under which the Additional Tier 1 Securities are to be issued.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The Additional Tier 1 Securities and the Indenture
are governed by, and shall be construed in accordance with, the laws of the State of New York, except for the subordination and waiver
of set-off provisions which are governed by, and shall be construed in accordance with, Scots law. The terms of the Additional Tier 1
Securities include those stated in the Indenture and those terms made part of the Indenture by reference to the U.S. Trust Indenture Act
of 1939, as amended (the &ldquo;<B>TIA</B>&rdquo;). The Bank of New York Mellon, acting through its London Branch, will serve as Trustee
under the Indenture and will initially act as Paying Agent, and The Bank of New York Mellon, London Branch, will act as calculation agent
(the &ldquo;<B>Calculation Agent</B>&rdquo;) for the Additional Tier 1 Securities. <FONT STYLE="background-color: white">The Bank of New
York Mellon SA/NV, Dublin Branch will act as registrar for the Additional Tier 1 Securities.</FONT></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The Additional Tier 1 Securities will constitute
our direct, unsecured, unguaranteed and subordinated obligations and will rank <I>pari passu</I> without any preference among themselves.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">The Additional Tier 1 Securities will be issued
in an aggregate principal amount of up to $1,000,000,000. We will issue the Additional Tier 1 Securities in fully registered form in denominations
of $200,000 and in integral multiples of $1,000 thereafter (the denomination of each book-entry interest being the &ldquo;<B>Tradable
Amount</B>&rdquo; of such book-entry interest). Prior to the Automatic Conversion (as defined below), the aggregate Tradable Amount of
the book-entry interests in each Additional Tier 1 Security shall be equal to such Additional Tier 1 Security&rsquo;s principal amount.
Following the Automatic Conversion, the principal amount of each Additional Tier 1 Security shall be zero (as described below under &ldquo;<I>&mdash;Conversion&mdash;Conversion
Procedures</I>&rdquo;).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">Upon issuance, the Additional Tier 1 Securities
will be represented by one or more fully registered global notes (&ldquo;<B>Global Notes</B>&rdquo;). Each such Global Note will be deposited
with, or on behalf of, The Depository Trust Company (the &ldquo;<B>DTC</B>&rdquo;). You will hold a beneficial interest in the Additional
Tier 1 Securities through DTC and its participants. LBG expects to deliver the Additional Tier 1 Securities through the facilities of
DTC on November 3, 2025.&nbsp;&nbsp;For a more detailed summary of the form of the Additional Tier 1 Securities and settlement and clearance
arrangements, see &ldquo;<I>&mdash;Form of Additional Tier 1 Securities, Clearance and Settlement</I>&rdquo;.&nbsp;&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">Indirect holders trading their beneficial interests
in the Additional Tier 1 Securities through DTC must trade in DTC&rsquo;s same-day funds settlement system and pay in immediately available
funds. Secondary market trading will occur in the ordinary way following the applicable rules and clearing system operating procedures
of DTC, including those of its indirect participants, Euroclear Bank SA/NV (&ldquo;<B>Euroclear</B>&rdquo;) and Clearstream Banking S.A.
(&ldquo;<B>Clearstream, Luxembourg</B>&rdquo;). Definitive securities will only be issued in limited circumstances described under &ldquo;<I>&mdash;Form
of Additional Tier 1 Securities, Clearance and Settlement</I>&rdquo;.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">Payment of principal of and interest, if any,
on the Additional Tier 1 Securities, so long as the Additional Tier 1 Securities are represented by the Global Notes, will be made in
immediately available funds. Beneficial interests in the Global Notes will trade in the same-day funds settlement system of DTC, and secondary
market trading activity in such interests will therefore settle in same-day funds. LBG currently expects such trading and settlement to
continue in the period between the Conversion Date and the Suspension Date (each as defined below).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>


