<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&ldquo;<B>Extraordinary Dividend</B>&rdquo; means
any Cash Dividend that is expressly declared by LBG to be a capital distribution, extraordinary dividend, extraordinary distribution,
special dividend, special distribution or return of value to its shareholders as a class or any analogous or similar term, in which case
the Extraordinary Dividend shall be such Cash Dividend.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&ldquo;<B>Cash Dividend</B>&rdquo; means any dividend
or distribution in respect of the Ordinary Shares which is to be paid or made to LBG&rsquo;s shareholders as a class in cash (in whatever
currency) and however described and whether payable out of share premium account, profits, retained earnings or any other capital or revenue
reserve or account, and including a distribution or payment to LBG&rsquo;s shareholders upon or in connection with a reduction of capital.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

